WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.819
No matter how different we are from each other,
everybody has a shadow.

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:10.470
It’s a constant companion, always with us
no matter where we go...Unless where we go

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.150
is a room with all of the lights off, of course.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:17.000
As a child, shadows seem mysterious or even
terrifying.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.330
But as we get older, we learn that shadows
are nothing to be concerned about, just your

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.000
body blocking light.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.170
Of course, at the SCP Foundation, nothing
is what it seems, and a shadow is never just

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.500
a shadow.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.899
Near an abandoned Air Force base in Afghanistan,
nestled next to a set of human remains, The

00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:41.570
Foundation discovered an unusual object capable
of turning a simple shadow into a prison.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:48.889
SCP-272 is an iron nail, 11.5 cm in length,
covered in engravings of an unknown origin.

00:00:48.889 --> 00:00:53.410
The engravings have not been identified or
traced to a specific civilization, but the

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:58.249
research staff assigned to the object has
described them as “captivating, but scary.”

00:00:58.249 --> 00:01:02.949
It was discovered during a sweep, pulled out
of a rock face by a member of Foundation personnel.

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:06.060
At first, he believed it to be an ordinary
nail.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.390
Until he dropped it.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.300
Suddenly, for no apparent reason, he was unable
to move from the spot.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.140
He stood there, calling out for help, for
20 minutes before another member of personnel

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.940
picked up the nail and he regained full range
of motion.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:25.090
SCP-272, like many other objects in Foundation
containment, is almost eerily mundane.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:28.920
Aside from the engravings on its surface,
the nail looks like any other nail you might

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.950
find scattered on the ground.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.100
Its true nature only reveals itself if you
happen to drop it.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.870
Determined to learn more about the nail’s
properties, limitations, and potential unknown

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:43.910
adverse effects, the Foundation conducted
a series of experiments.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:48.980
The first experiment was conducted at the
discovery site for SCP-272, the rock face

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.360
in Afghanistan.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:56.190
A D-Class, referred to as D-272-01, was handed
the nail and instructed to hammer it into

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.920
his shadow, in the area of his feet.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.950
Once the nail was 2/3 into the rock, 01 was
no longer able to move.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.570
He attempted to run, but could not lift his
feet.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:11.180
He stood there, sweating and immobile, until
he collapsed from heatstroke.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.749
At this point, a researcher intervened and
attempted to carry the unconscious man out

00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:15.819
of the sun.

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:20.829
No matter how hard they tried, his body could
not be moved until they removed the nail.

00:02:20.829 --> 00:02:25.650
01 was taken to a hospital and administered
fluids and a medical exam, and testing was

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.489
suspended for the day.

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:31.680
After determining that the nail immobilizes
its victims by trapping their shadow, and

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.909
them, in place, the research team wanted to
test the limitations of this effect.

00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:41.659
If the nail needs a shadow to work, then what
happens when there is no shadow present?

00:02:41.659 --> 00:02:46.209
A new D-class, 02, was selected and brought
to the same discovery site.

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:49.939
This time, however, they went after dark at
approximately 10 PM.

00:02:49.939 --> 00:02:54.519
The nail was dropped at 02’s feet, and embedded
itself in the earth without needing to be

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:55.519
hammered.

00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:58.959
Then, 02 was instructed to walk 10 meters
away from the nail.

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:02.010
He managed this easily, with no adverse effects.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:06.129
The experiment was relatively uneventful,
until 02 attempted to flee the scene and was

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:08.439
terminated for his escape attempt.

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:12.639
The body was disposed of, and the research
team made note of their findings: the nail

00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:16.349
does not work if the subject is not casting
a shadow.

00:03:16.349 --> 00:03:21.909
So, if total darkness kept the nail from working,
and bright light meant it worked completely,

00:03:21.909 --> 00:03:25.329
what would happen if the light changed in
the middle of the experiment?

00:03:25.329 --> 00:03:30.200
Two hours before sunrise, the very same night,
another D-Class was brought to the site.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.480
The subject, 03, was instructed to walk away
from the nail in a straight line until he

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.900
was told to stop.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.780
Two hours later, when the sun came up, all
hell broke loose.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.629
03 was pulled into pieces as his body attempted
to make its way back to the direction of the

00:03:44.629 --> 00:03:46.939
nail by any means necessary.

00:03:46.939 --> 00:03:51.139
His legs were yanked back toward the nail
and were collected several feet from it.

00:03:51.139 --> 00:03:56.349
His torso, on the other hand, was located
106 meters away from the nail, with signs

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:58.769
of road rash and severe trauma.

00:03:58.769 --> 00:04:02.849
Three clean-up teams were required to remove
all evidence of the carnage, the nail was

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:09.129
removed to test facility 25-h, and the team
decided to put an end to any further experimentation

00:04:09.129 --> 00:04:11.159
involving sunrise.

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:14.920
Several lighting-based experiments followed
the sunrise disaster, all with relatively

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.590
uneventful findings.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:21.250
The research continued in this way, until
one member of the research team, Dr. Cho,

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:27.570
posited a new question: What happens if the
nail is embedded in two overlapping shadows?

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:33.190
Two other members of D-Class personnel, 04
and 05, were positioned under stadium lights

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.170
so that their shadows overlapped.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.280
The nail was dropped onto a point where the
shadows were on top of each other, and promptly

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.070
embedded itself in the ground.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:44.450
Both subjects were instructed to attempt to
move away from the nail.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.670
05 was completely trapped, unable to move
her feet or walk away.

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:53.150
Meanwhile, 04 was able to move freely with
no consequences except for the feeling of

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.150
a “chill.”

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:57.850
So, the nail is only able to hold one person
at a time.

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:01.970
In an attempt to see if there is a pattern
present in terms of which person the nail

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:06.700
will hold, if presented with multiple options,
a follow-up experiment was conducted with

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:12.410
eight members of D-class personnel, ranging
in age from 18 to 59 years old.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.230
All eight subjects were placed with their
shadows overlapping, and the nail was dropped

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.020
onto the point of overlap.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:22.140
The youngest subject, an 18 year old boy,
was held still by the nail.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:26.500
The other seven test subjects let out a scream
when the nail hit the ground, and were reported

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.010
to shiver throughout the duration of the test.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:33.650
When the 18-year-old was taken out of the
study, and the experiment repeated, the second-youngest

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.940
person in the group was held in place.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:41.240
The experiment was repeated four more times,
removing a subject each time, until Subject

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.370
07 collapsed from hypothermia.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:47.780
The next experiment was conducted outside,
in a grassy field near the test site.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.360
Subject 05 was placed on the grass and handed
a shovel.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.620
Once the nail was firmly in the subject’s
shadow, she was instructed to dig it out of

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.620
the dirt.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.040
05 began digging and proceeded normally at
first.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.450
After 90 seconds, however, she fell to the
ground, screaming in agony.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:07.870
A medic rushed to her side, but by the time
he reached her she was already dead.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:13.410
An autopsy determined that Subject 05 died
of a cerebral hemorrhage with no clear physical

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.910
cause, though it was apparent that the attempt
to remove the nail is what killed her.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.850
The research team decided to take a break
from human trials and take a closer look at

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.810
the physical properties of the nail itself.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:26.770
What weaknesses did it have?

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.770
Could it be destroyed?

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:33.290
Subject 09 was given the nail and a collection
of tools, then instructed to “go to town”

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.070
on the object and attempt to destroy it.

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:40.520
09 placed the nail in a vice, and attempted
to go at it with an angle grinder.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:45.300
As soon as the grinder touched the nail, 09
fell to the ground, seizing and speaking in

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.050
tongues, hands pressed to his temples.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:53.090
30 seconds later, he was dead from the same
kind of cerebral hemorrhage that killed Subject

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.090
05.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:58.320
Examination of the nail revealed a small amount
of surface damage, showing that the nail likely

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:03.220
can be destroyed, but is somehow able to defend
itself against destruction.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:07.640
Regular human trials were resumed the next
day, and Subject 10 was brought into the test

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:08.640
facility.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:14.100
There, one stadium light was placed on a computer-controlled
track, allowing the light to be shifted incrementally

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.500
from a remote point outside of the room.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:20.750
The light was set up to cast a long shadow,
and the nail was dropped into the shadow’s

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.750
head.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.010
Immediately, Subject 10 was unable to walk
away from the nail, in keeping with the standard

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.740
effects of SCP-272.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:31.120
Then, the light was slowly raised, moving
the shadow.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:35.210
The subject was dragged along as the shadow
moved, as if yanked by his feet.

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:37.580
He stumbled and had to work to regain his
balance.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:39.330
Then, the light was moved quickly.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.700
Again, the subject was dragged along with
the motion of the shadow.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:46.860
However, due to the rapid pace of the light’s
motion, he was unable to keep his balance

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.230
and fell to the floor, receiving scrapes,
bruises, and mild road rash.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:56.210
Finally, in an attempt to see what might happen
if the subject was unable to move even against

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:58.889
his will, 10 was restrained.

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:02.639
His feet were chained to the floor, and a
chicken wire screen was placed between him

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:03.639
and the nail.

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:05.600
Then, the light was moved again.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.730
To the horror of the research team watching,
these restraints did nothing to lessen the

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.400
nail’s hold on the subject.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.290
He was pulled forward violently, the chains
ripped from the floor, and his body slowly

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:20.860
forced itself through the chicken wire, landing
on the other side in a pile of tiny pieces,

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.210
like a potato shot through a tennis racquet.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:27.760
No matter what is holding them down, or what
is in their way, a subject cannot escape the

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.960
pull of their shadow, or the prison of the
nail.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.740
They will be bound to it, even if it kills
them.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:38.460
Testing was temporarily suspended while a
cleaning crew attended to the room, taking

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.440
the rest of the day to get the bloodstains
out of the concrete.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:45.100
The final experiment on record was conducted
the following day.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:50.300
Subject D-272-04 was placed in the center
of the room, with one stadium light casting

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.770
his shadow at a 45-degree angle.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:56.200
The nail was dropped onto 04’s shadow, and
he was held in place.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.150
Then, the research team simply waited.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:03.350
Food and water was provided every few hours,
as well as a bucket to use as a bathroom.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:08.650
For the first two days, the subject seemed
relatively normal, if exhausted and upset.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:12.280
On the third day, he did not respond to food
or water when it was offered.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.730
After a week had passed, the subject began
to speak in rapid, manic streams of what was

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:19.029
determined to be a dead language.

00:09:19.029 --> 00:09:22.870
By day eleven, the subject was switching back
and forth between bursts of intense ranting

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:24.810
and a catatonic state.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:30.760
Finally, after fourteen days pinned to the
spot by the nail, Subject 04 was set free.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.590
As soon as the nail was removed, they began
speaking English again.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.920
They were severely malnourished and visibly
traumatized but immediately began to recover

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.020
once freed from the nail’s hold.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:45.360
Portions of the subject’s rants were recorded
and translated by Dr. Kimiro, who attempted

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:48.140
to interview the subject on the fourteenth
day of the study.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:53.940
At one point, the subject said: “I cannot
sleep, the screams are heard, I am not warm,

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.380
the shadow steals.”

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:59.100
When asked how he was feeling, the subject
began to tear at the skin on his arms and

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:04.980
shout: “I am the prisoner of my own foolishness…let
my flesh crumble like the apple whose ashes

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.710
burn at my tongue.”

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:10.820
Not the most cheerful thing to hear, but not
too out of the ordinary for a day’s work

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:13.330
at the SCP Foundation either.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:19.630
Following this experiment, human experimentation
with SCP-272 was suspended until further notice.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:25.010
SCP-272 is kept in a small wooden box, hidden
in a vault at Sector-25.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:29.480
Because nothing happens to the object as long
as it is left alone, no further containment

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.480
procedures are considered necessary.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.100
When the nail is removed from containment
for experimentation, staff have been instructed

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:39.020
to take extra care not to drop it.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:44.570
SCP-272 is considered a “safe” class SCP,
due to its inability to act on its own.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:47.190
It does not appear to do anything when left
alone.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:51.500
However, there is clearly a great deal more
to that little nail than meets the eye.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:56.190
Somehow, it is able to wreak psychic havoc
on those it traps, and on anyone who might

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.280
try to harm it.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:02.480
The more we learn about the nature of SCP-272,
the more questions crop up.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.820
Where did it come from?

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:06.310
How does it get inside people’s heads?

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:09.910
What did Subject 04 mean by, “the shadow
steals”?

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:11.090
We may never know.

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:16.170
But, if you find yourself picking up any strange
nails one of these days, make sure you don’t

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:17.170
drop them.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:22.910
Now go check out “SCP-999 - The Tickle Monster”
and “SCP-978 - Desire Camera” for more

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.810
of our favorite Safe-Class SCPs!

